Rockchip vendor dma-buf heap stack (rk_dma_heap + rk-cma-heap) for 5.4.

Back-ported from the Rockchip develop-5.10 vendor tree
(drivers/dma-buf/rk_heaps/).  Builds rk-dma-heap.ko (the heap framework,
provides rk_dma_heap_find()) and rk-cma-heap.ko (the CMA heap backend, which
registers the "rk-dma-heap-cma" heap that drivers/rknpu looks up).

Both are modules (tristate, =m) and stay out of the boot path.

Necessary core changes (a module cannot reference unexported symbols):
  * mm/cma.c: EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(cma_alloc/cma_release)
  * kernel/dma/contiguous.c: EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(dma_contiguous_default_area)
  * mm/init-mm.c: EXPORT_SYMBOL(init_mm)
  * mm/vmalloc.c: EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(get_vm_area_caller)

Config-5.4 additions (not part of this patch):
  CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_ROCKCHIP=m
  CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_ROCKCHIP_CMA_HEAP=m
  CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_ROCKCHIP_CMA_ALIGNMENT=8

Note: drivers/rknpu is built-in (=y) and links against rk_dma_heap_find(); a
modular heap can only satisfy it if rknpu is built as a module too
(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_RKNPU=m).

